# Open Work

Source-controlled backlog for unfinished implementation, cleanup, and operating work. Work that cannot proceed until the user chooses between options belongs in [OPEN_DECISIONS.md](OPEN_DECISIONS.md) instead.

## Status Values

| Status | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `open` | Work remains and is not currently blocked. |
| `blocked` | Work cannot proceed until a named decision, dependency, or condition resolves. |
| `in_progress` | Work has started and should be completed or deliberately paused. |
| `done` | The behavior is specified in its owner doc, code cites the relevant `{{ID_PREFIX}}-*` identifier, tests cover it, lint/type checks pass, and a completion judgment has been recorded for the relevant requirement ID(s) in `docs/technical/05-implementation-index.md`'s `Completion Judgment` column. `CHANGELOG.md` is updated. |
| `deferred` | Intentionally not part of the current scope. |

Sweep `done` rows out on the next cleanup pass — but only after the completion judgment is recorded in `docs/technical/05-implementation-index.md`. This file tracks what's outstanding, not a permanent record of everything ever finished; that record lives in the index instead, and it is never swept.

